  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C is implicated in the biological activity of NH-6 through a series of molecular interactions that involve a sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence suggests that Divaricataester C directly targets CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is then targeted by additional compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and 1-Hydroxycyclocolorenone, all of which ultimately lead to the targeting of NH-6. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Divaricataester C may influence the activity of the sialyltransferase, which in turn affects the production or modification of NH-6. The evidence supports a chain of interactions that links Divaricataester C to NH-6 through the sialyltransferase pathway, suggesting a possible role in modulating the biological activity of NH-6.",
